From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:29:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): fold the phone drawer's primary nav into one strip

On a phone, the drawer's primary nav is a stack of 44px rows above the
session list. In the overlay drawer the core destinations (New session,
Automations, Workflows, Inbox) now share one strip of equal-width
icon-over-label cells (at least 44px tall) in a rounded glass container:
three or four rows of 134px to 179px become a strip of about 68px.
Automations and Workflows keep their gates, so the strip has two to four
cells in the order of the rows. The strip never scrolls: Canvas, Usage and
extension pages, when enabled, stay full-width rows directly below it.
Cell labels follow the Appearance interface font size.

Every item now renders through PrimaryNavLink, which takes a row or cell
layout, so both layouts share one definition per destination; a small
PrimaryNavStrip wraps the core destinations only on the phone drawer. The
cells keep their test ids, component ids, links, drawer closing and active
highlight; New keeps the accessible name "New session" and its
aria-keyshortcuts, and the Inbox count sits on the cell's corner with the
same label. The strip follows the overlay drawer; the desktop layout and
a mobile-layout window that docks the sidebar beside the chat keep the
stacked rows.

Refs #13482

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/mobile-sidebar-nav-strip; drop this copy once it merges.

